\begin{array} { l l l } { T _ { 0 } ^ { i } } & { = } & { - ( { \bar { \rho } } + { \bar { p } } ) ( v ^ { i } - B ^ { i } ) / a } \end{array}\tag{131}
$$  
$$
T _ { j } ^ { i } = \delta _ { j } ^ { i } ( \bar { p } + \delta p ) + \Sigma _ { j } ^ { i } .\tag{132}
$$  
The anisotropic stress $\Sigma _ { j } ^ { i }$ is gauge-invariant while the density, pressure and momentum density $( ( \delta q ) _ { , i } \equiv ( \bar { \rho } + \bar { p } ) v _ { i } )$ transform as follows  
$$
\delta \rho \quad \to \quad \delta \rho - \dot { \bar { \rho } } \alpha\tag{133}
$$  
$$
\delta p \quad \to \quad \delta p - { \dot { \bar { p } } } \alpha\tag{134}
